---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

import dashboardRepairImage from '@/assets/dashboard-leather-repair/dashboard-repair.jpg';
import processSpecialistImage from '@/assets/dashboard-leather-repair/process-specialist.jpg';
import processDismantledImage from '@/assets/dashboard-leather-repair/process-dismantled.jpg';
import processFittingImage from '@/assets/dashboard-leather-repair/process-fitting.jpg';
import dashboardRewrapImage from '@/assets/dashboard-leather-repair/dashboard-rewrap.jpeg';
import beforeAfterBmwImage from '@/assets/dashboard-leather-repair/before-after-bmw.png';
import beforeAfterHyundaiImage from '@/assets/dashboard-leather-repair/before-after-hyundai.png';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <title>Car Dashboard Leather Repair in Singapore | Five Star Auto Leather</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Cracked, peeling, or sun-damaged dashboard? We provide professional car dashboard leather repair and reupholstery services in Singapore. Book now!"
    />
  </Fragment>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="order-2 sm:order-1">
      <Image
        src={dashboardRepairImage}
        alt="Honda Stepwagon Spada dashboard finished with two-tone black and blue car dashboard leather repair"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
        widths={[800]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="custom-featured h-full w-full bg-black object-cover"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="order-1 flex items-center justify-center bg-black px-4 py-8 sm:order-2 sm:px-16">
      <div
        class="title-slide-up flex h-full flex-col items-center justify-center text-center text-white sm:items-start sm:text-left"
      >
        <h1 class="text-4xl">Professional Car Dashboard Leather Repair in Singapore</h1>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Singapore's UV rays and heat cause your dashboard to crack, bubble or peel. Five Star
          reupholsters dashboards using premium materials matched to your vehicle. We restore
          dashboards to showroom quality, helping protect your car's resale value.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/contact-us"
          class="mt-8 inline-block w-36 rounded bg-red-700 px-4 py-2 text-center text-sm font-medium transition-colors hover:bg-red-600"
        >
          Get in Touch
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-7xl flex-col items-center gap-8 px-4 py-8 sm:px-6">
    <div class="text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl">The Problem: Why Dashboards Deteriorate</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Singapore's tropical climate is harsh on interior materials. Here's what typically happens:
      </p>
    </div>

    <table class="w-full border-collapse border border-gray-300">
      <thead>
        <tr class="bg-gray-100">
          <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3 text-left">Symptom</th>
          <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3 text-left">Cause</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Cracking on the top surface</td>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
            >Prolonged UV exposure hardens and shrinks the leather or PVC surface</td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Bubbling or peeling near the windscreen</td>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
            >Heat causes adhesive to fail, especially on afternoon-facing dashboards</td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Fading or discolouration</td>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
            >Sunlight bleaches dyes unevenly, leaving patchy colour</td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Sticky or gummy surface</td>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
            >Lower-quality dashboard materials degrading in heat</td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Curling edges near window seals</td>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Thermal expansion over time</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="text-center">
      Most factory dashboards use a thin layer of leather or PVC bonded over foam. That foam breaks
      down in 5 to 8 years depending on sun exposure. All these issues are fixable.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-6">
      <Image
        src={processSpecialistImage}
        alt="Specialist installing a newly wrapped Hyundai i30 dashboard back onto the vehicle frame during car dashboard leather repair"
        loading="lazy"
        widths={[640, 1280]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="h-full w-full object-cover"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col justify-center px-4 py-8 lg:col-span-6 lg:px-16">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-center text-2xl lg:text-left">Our Dashboard Restoration Process</h2>
      <p class="mb-8 text-center lg:text-left">
        Our car dashboard leather repair process is handled entirely in-house, from removal and
        preparation to the final quality check. Watch how a full rewrap is done at Five Star Auto
        Leather.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 1: Free Assessment & Quote</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Bring your vehicle in for a complimentary dashboard assessment. Our specialists will inspect
        your dashboard's condition and provide a customised quotation based on its material, damage
        severity, and the complexity of dismantling and reinstallation.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 2: Surface Preparation</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Before rewrapping, the dashboard is thoroughly cleaned and degreased so the new material
        adheres properly. Worn, peeling or damaged areas are carefully sanded and prepared. Where
        necessary, cracks and deeper imperfections are repaired using a specialised filler compound
        to create a smooth, even surface.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 3: Precision Rewrap</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Using high-temperature resistant and formaldehyde-free industrial adhesives designed for
        Singapore's tropical climate, we apply the new material carefully for a smooth, wrinkle-free
        finish. Every section is carefully bonded to eliminate bubbles, ripples and lifting.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 4: Reassembly & Quality Check</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Once the rewrap is complete, all air vents, buttons, trim pieces and sensors are carefully
        reinstalled. We carry out a full quality inspection covering fitment, alignment, finish and
        colour consistency before handing the vehicle back to you.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Typical turnaround:</strong> 2–3 working days, depending on the extent of damage and
        the complexity of dashboard removal and reinstallation
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    class="col-span-full mx-auto grid w-full max-w-7xl grid-cols-1 gap-3 px-4 py-8 sm:grid-cols-2 sm:px-6"
  >
    <Image
      src={processDismantledImage}
      alt="Fully dismantled Hyundai dashboard and centre console exposed for car dashboard leather repair"
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
      widths={[640, 1280]}
      sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
      class="h-full w-full rounded-lg bg-black object-cover"
    />
    <Image
      src={processFittingImage}
      alt="Technician's hands fitting control buttons into a freshly wrapped suede-textured dashboard during car dashboard leather repair"
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
      widths={[640, 1280]}
      sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
      class="h-full w-full rounded-lg bg-black object-cover"
    />
  </section>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="flex flex-col justify-center px-4 py-8 md:px-16">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-center text-2xl">Why Choose Five Star Auto Leather?</h2>
      <p class="mb-8 text-center">
        Choosing the right specialist for car dashboard leather repair means looking at how a
        workshop prices its work, manages your car's downtime, sources its materials, and controls
        quality. Five Star Auto Leather does all of this in-house.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Transparent Pricing</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Every dashboard rewrap is individually quoted based on your vehicle model, dashboard
        condition, chosen material and the complexity of the work involved. No misleading "from"
        prices or hidden charges — just fair, transparent pricing tailored to your vehicle.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Minimising Downtime</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Dashboard rewrapping is one of the more labour-intensive interior restoration jobs and
        typically takes 2–3 working days (longer for certain luxury and supercar models). If you're
        also reupholstering your seats, steering wheel or other interior components, we'll complete
        everything together whenever possible to minimise your vehicle's downtime.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Built for Singapore's Climate</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        We use premium automotive upholstery materials that are heat and UV resistant, paired with
        high-performance adhesives where required. Designed to withstand Singapore's tropical
        climate, your newly rewrapped dashboard is built to maintain its appearance and durability
        for years to come.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">100% In-House Craftsmanship</h3>
      <p>
        Every dashboard is rewrapped by our experienced craftsmen at our Singapore workshop — never
        outsourced. From careful preparation and precision rewrap to final installation, we maintain
        complete quality control and back our work with a workmanship warranty for your peace of
        mind.
      </p>
    </div>

    <Image
      src={dashboardRewrapImage}
      alt="Toyota Corolla Cross interior with car dashboard leather repair in rich caramel, complemented by matching front seat car upholstery"
      loading="lazy"
      widths={[640, 1280]}
      sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
      class="h-full w-full object-cover"
    />
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-7xl flex-col items-center gap-8 px-4 py-8 sm:px-6">
    <h2 class="text-2xl">Before & After</h2>

    <div class="grid w-full gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <Image
        src={beforeAfterBmwImage}
        alt="BMW 630i dashboard before and after car dashboard leather repair, showing removal of cracked red leather and installation of a fresh black suede-textured finish"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
        widths={[640, 1280]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="w-full rounded-lg object-cover"
      />
      <Image
        src={beforeAfterHyundaiImage}
        alt="Hyundai i30 dashboard before and after car dashboard leather repair, transforming a cracked factory finish into a premium black suede-textured surface"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
        widths={[640, 1280]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="w-full rounded-lg object-cover"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-black">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-7xl flex-col gap-8 px-4 py-8 text-white sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="text-center text-2xl">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">Do you have to remove the entire dashboard to rewrap it?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Yes, in most cases. Removing the dashboard allows us to properly prepare the surface and
          wrap it seamlessly around edges and contours, resulting in a much cleaner, longer-lasting
          finish. This is also why dashboard rewrapping is one of the most labour-intensive interior
          upholstery services.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          For certain vehicles where only a removable trim section is damaged, we may only need to
          remove that specific panel instead of the entire dashboard.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">How long does dashboard rewrapping take?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Most dashboard rewraps take 2–3 working days. Luxury vehicles, supercars and models with
          more complex dashboard designs may require additional time due to the greater dismantling
          complexity and more intricate craftsmanship involved.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">Will the new dashboard match my original colour?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We aim to achieve the closest possible match using our extensive range of automotive
          upholstery materials and colours. While we cannot always guarantee an exact factory match,
          we can usually achieve a finish that closely resembles your original interior.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">Can I change my dashboard to a different colour?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Absolutely. Dashboard rewrapping gives you the freedom to customise your interior to match
          your seats, steering wheel, door panels or your personal style.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          However, because the dashboard sits directly beneath the windscreen, we generally
          recommend darker or more muted colours to minimise reflections and glare while driving.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">Is dashboard rewrapping cheaper than replacing the dashboard?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">Not necessarily. The answer depends on your vehicle.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Dashboard rewrapping is a highly labour-intensive process involving dismantling, surface
          preparation, template making, upholstery fabrication, stitching, wrapping and
          reinstallation. For some vehicles, especially where replacement dashboards are readily
          available, replacement may cost a similar amount or even less.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          However, for many premium, older or discontinued models where replacement dashboards are
          expensive or difficult to source, rewrapping can be the more practical and cost-effective
          option. During our assessment, we'll be happy to advise which solution makes the most
          sense for your vehicle.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <iframe
    src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3988.6660102489027!2d103.8690919!3d1.3770706000000001!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x31da1658b06d3b7d%3A0xbb4992fe537bc610!2sFive%20Star%20Auto%20Leather!5e0!3m2!1sen!2ssg!4v1766728446154!5m2!1sen!2ssg"
    width="100%"
    height="400"
    style="border:0;"
    allowfullscreen=""
    loading="lazy"
    referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"></iframe>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h2 {
    font-family: 'RacingSansOne', var(--font-sans);
  }
</style>
